 Real-Time ArgoCD Error: “Out of Sync” – What I Learned 🔄

Faced a real-time issue today while working with ArgoCD —
 my application kept showing “Out of Sync” even though the Git repo looked perfectly fine 😅

Here’s what I found after some digging 👇

🔍 Root Cause:
 The cluster had a few manual changes applied directly using kubectl.
 ArgoCD detected a drift between the live state (in cluster) and the desired state (in Git).

💡 Fix:
 Simply ran the sync command:

argocd app sync <app-name>

and ArgoCD immediately restored the desired state from Git ✅

💬 Lesson Learned:
 Never make manual edits in the cluster when using GitOps.
 Your Git repo is the single source of truth, and ArgoCD will always reconcile to match it.

That’s the beauty (and the discipline) of GitOps — everything is versioned, auditable, and consistent 🚀
